question:
What will be the output of the following code?
```python
class A:
    def __init__(self):
        self._x = 5

    @property
    def x(self):
        return self._x

    @x.setter
    def x(self, value):
        self._x = value

class B(A):
    @A.x.setter
    def x(self, value):
        if value < 0:
            raise ValueError('Value must be non-negative')
        super(B, B).x.__set__(self, value) # Fixed line

b = B()
b.x = 10
print(b.x)
```

